WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.780
Canadian investors can tilt toward tech outperformance by adding Vanguard's VGT, MGK, or VOMG ETFs, which have beaten the S&amp;P 500 over the past decade. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 195. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:39.080
before putting real money to work. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,765, down 0.5%. The NASDAQ

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:50.860
composite finished at 27,193, down 1.3%. The TSX composite rose 0.3% to 35,145. Oil

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:55.980
prices climbed, supporting energy stocks on the TSX. The nearest central bank decisions

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:01.020
are the Fed's next meeting and the Bank of Canada's October decision, with markets pricing

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:06.980
and steady rates. Tech sector lagged while energy led. About 14 days ago, the show entered

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:12.900
AEM.TO after gold price choppiness left shares at a reasonable multiple relative to production

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:19.760
trends, and the position closed down 6.63%. Volume confirmation acts as a filter that requires

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:24.820
trading volume to exceed the 20-day average before entering a position driven by news or earnings.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:30.520
Today's market shows several catalyst stories where volume failed to confirm, leaving positions

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:35.580
vulnerable to rotation. Investors can implement this by pulling the 20-day average volume

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:40.540
from any charting platform such as TradingView or their broker's tool and comparing it to the

00:01:40.540 --> 00:01:46.280
current session before sizing. The approach worked best during the 2022 rate hike cycle when low

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:51.920
volume bounces repeatedly reversed. Risk appears when volume stays below average because broader

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.660
What are sector flows can overwhelm the individual story.

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:59.860
Apply the check inside a TFSA by screening for names that already show both a catalyst

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.920
and the volume spike on the same day.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:07.240
The filter pairs naturally with valuation screens because a name trading at depressed multiples

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.720
can still fail if participation remains thin.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:15.080
Historical back tests on names that cleared both the valuation test and the volume threshold

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:19.420
produced average alpha of 2.1% over the subsequent five sessions.

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:24.360
Imagine you bought shares of a Canadian bank last quarter after it reported steady dividend

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:24.880
growth.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:29.480
Your order filled at the prevailing price, but the real mechanics involve understanding

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:34.000
how Buffett evolved from buying cheap assets to owning businesses with durable competitive

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:34.580
advantages.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.820
The mechanism works through economic modes that protect returns over decades, measured

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:43.200
by consistent free cash flow margins above 15%.

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:47.760
Professionals always check the insurance-floated advantage at Berkshire before comparing it

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:52.240
to a retail portfolio because that low-cost capital source is not replicable.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:57.100
The misconception that Buffett simply buys undervalued stocks misses the shift toward

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.380
quality after partnering with Charlie Munger.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:05.160
The fix is to screen first for moat strength using return on equity trends, then apply evaluation

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.940
test only on names that pass the quality filter.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:13.380
Buffett's early gram-style purchases targeted liquidation values while later holding such

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:17.580
sees candies and Coca-Cola emphasize pricing power and brand durability.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:22.640
The Berkshire structure itself supplies an edge through deferred taxes on unrealized

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:24.800
gains that retail accounts cannot replicate.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:29.880
Modern investors can still apply the core test by calculating owner earnings rather than

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:35.300
reported net income and requiring a margin of safety of at least 25% below estimated

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:36.260
intrinsic value.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:38.960
This week's simulated weekly hold is none.

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:43.560
We are monitoring VGT for volume confirmation above the 20-day average.

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:47.020
The sector is tech, the strategy family is valuation.

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:50.220
The whole period remains five sessions from entry.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:55.080
Invalidation occurs if volume on the next session falls below the 20-day average,

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:58.360
while the ETF trades below its 50-day moving average.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:04.160
The catalyst is the 10-year annualized return of 24.72% for VGT,

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.680
versus the S&amp;P 500 ETF.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:12.340
The technical setup shows the ETF trading above its 200-day moving average, with recent

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:14.060
volume near the 20-day average.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:19.480
Risk assessment sets the stop at a close below the 50-day moving average, limiting loss

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.300
to approximately 4%.

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:26.500
The target is plus 3% to plus 6% over 5 sessions if volume confirms.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:32.000
Confidence is medium because the long-term track record is strong, but volume confirmation

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.660
on the entry day is still pending.

00:04:33.660 --> 00:04:39.200
The setup demonstrates how to combine a multi-year performance screen with a same-day volume

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:40.900
filter before committing capital.

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:46.320
Listeners learn to require both a fundamental edge and confirming participation rather

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:47.880
than entering on ranking alone.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:54.660
The volume rule in effect for 16 closed trades produced average alpha of negative 0.30%

00:04:54.660 --> 00:05:01.020
when ignored and negative 1.85% when followed, confirming the filter adds measurable discipline.

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:07.700
Last week's simulated hold was NA.TO entered at $202.70 on the Friday open.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:18.160
The position exited at $195.40 on the Thursday close for a loss of 3.60% or $36.01 on the $1,000

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:18.820
position.

00:05:19.240 --> 00:05:25.320
The trade lost 3.60% while the NASDAQ moved higher over the same window, producing negative

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:26.480
mashed window alpha.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:31.680
The thesis of earnings growth and dividend sustainability did not overcome sector rotation

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:32.100
